{{Quote|Grants regenerative abilities, powerful fire-based attacks, and the ability to transform into full body Phoenix.|Shop}}
'''Phoenix''' (formerly known as '''Bird: Phoenix''') is a {{Legendary}} [[Beast]]-type [[Blox Fruit]] that costs {{Money|1,800,000}} or {{Robux|2,000}} from the [[Blox Fruit Dealer]].

Phoenix grants the user the ability to manipulate blue and yellow flames with magical properties. It's best known for its lethal regenerative ability, allowing the user to heal [[Allying|Allies]] and themselves while repelling enemies at the same time. The fruit also allows the user to transform into a full-form phoenix, granting them the ability to fly freely and attack enemies while airborne.

==Awakening==
Phoenix costs {{Fragment|18,500}} to fully [[Raids|awaken]].

"The Phoenix" [[Titles|title]] #041 will be granted upon awakening at least one move of this fruit.

{{Awakening Price Table
|move1 = Z  | 500
|move2 = F  | 2,000
|move3 = X  | 3,000
|move4 = C  | 4,000
|move5 = M1 | 4,000
|move6 = V  | 5,000
}}

===Unlocking Phoenix Raid===
Phoenix has a unique [[Raids|awakening]] method that differs from other [[Blox Fruits|fruits]]. Normally, players must purchase a [[Microchip|chip]] from the [[Mysterious Scientist]], but the process for this fruit is different. The player will need to:
# Obtain 400+ mastery on Phoenix.
# Talk to [[Sick Scientist]], who is located at the [[Sea of Treats]]. The [[Microchip|Raid Chip]] can also be purchased through the [[Mysterious Scientist]], even in the [[Second Sea]], after the player has purchased it at least one time from the [[Sick Scientist]]. 
#* This NPC will sell the player the Phoenix [[Microchip|raid chip]] for {{Fragment|1,000}} or a [[Blox Fruits|physical fruit]] worth at least {{Money|1,000,000}} or more.
#* Purchasing a [[Microchip|chip]] with {{Fragment|Fragments}} has a 2-hour cooldown, just like the [[Mysterious Scientist]].
#* The quest is ''permanent'', so when the player switches to another [[Blox Fruits|fruit]], the player can still buy the [[Raids|Phoenix Raid Chip]].

''Note: Players can still join Phoenix [[raids]] hosted by other players and [[Raids|awaken]] Phoenix without having 400+ mastery, so the user can ask other players for help if they haven’t gotten 400+ mastery.''

