==Trivia==
* Currently, [[Buddha]] and Phoenix are the only [[Beast]]-type fruits to have an [[Raids|awakening]].
** Phoenix had some of the single harshest nerfs of any fruit, it's effects still hampering performance even today. Most moves have much larger visuals than actual hitboxes, attacks fire slow, endlag was added, and even moves can't chain well. The M1's drag hitbox is also noticeably smaller than before.
* Because of the Phoenix Flames and Feathers' Immortality passive on the {{Ability|F|2}} move, the user can stall above enemies and damage them, making it an ideal way to AFK farm [[money]]/[[mastery]].
** [[Smoke]] and [[Blizzard]] also technically have infinite damage moves, but their moves need to be held.
* Phoenix is the first fruit to have a Mastery Requirement in order to obtain a chip for a [[Raids|raid]].
* Phoenix is one of the few fruits to have ranged M1s.
* Unawakened {{Ability|X}} heals at a quicker rate than the awakened {{Ability|X|2}}.
* Phoenix is the first fruit to possess [[health]] benefits. (excluding pre-nerf [[Buddha]])
* The transformed Phoenix resembles a creature found in Chinese myths known as {{w|Fenghuang}}. The Phoenix is supposed to be a symbol of grace and virtue, an immortal bird that represented beauty. Its Blox Fruits counterpart, however, depicts the Phoenix as a violent and fiery beast. This depiction is closer to the Western Phoenix, despite having the traits and features of the Fenghuang.
* {{Ability|F|1}} can be used to damage [[Shark]]s or the [[Leviathan]] while other players are attacking just by still staying on top.
* If the player uses awakened {{Ability|C|2}} or {{Ability|Z|2}} while using the unawakened transformation, the transformation will be cancelled.
* If the player starts using the transformed [X] move before being kicked out of transformation via low energy, they will use the transformed version instead of the normal [X] move.
* Awakened Phoenix's {{Ability|X|2}} can be used with the unawakened {{Ability|V}}. If used with transformation, it will make the user's speed become a little slower.
* Holding the unawakened [X] move is a highly recommended way to get the [[Titles|title]] "Empty Vessel".
* Phoenix is the first fruit that can transform without a fury meter, the second being [[Leopard]], the third being [[Mammoth]] and the fourth being [[Yeti]].
* [[Sea Beast]]s will appear in a Phoenix raid, specifically on the 4th and 5th islands. These Sea Beasts do not drop anything and are optional to fight during the raid, as only the enemies '''on the raid island''' are required to progress to the next island. However, it is advised to defeat these Sea Beasts if possible, as they pose as extreme threats to those on the raid island. Fruits such as [[Buddha]] and [[Yeti]] are recommended against these Sea Beasts. Moving a significant distance away from the island and remaining there for 20-30 seconds will cause these Sea Beasts to despawn.
* When paired with [[Ghoul|Blood Siphon]] ([[Gears|Gear]] 2), the [[Lei]] accessory, gathering 5–8 enemies then using [[Skull Guitar]] [X] with the Vampiric III [[Enchantments|enchant]], and activating {{Ability|X|2}} can result in the fastest [[Health|health regeneration]] within the game.
* Although Phoenix and [[Portal]] share the robux price of ({{Robux|2,000}}), they do not share the same {{Money|Money}} value. Phoenix is valued at {{Money|1,800,000}} and [[Portal]] is valued at {{Money|1,900,000}}.
* In awakened form, due to the 33% [[health]] rule, if the player resets their character or dies while transformed, they will untransform before dying, unlike other beast fruits.
* Phoenix is the only fruit with a transformation that can be ended in a way other than emptying a fury meter. (This way being having below 33% [[health]] or [[energy]]).
* Phoenix has one of the oldest unreworked icons in the game.
* {{Ability|F|2}} will deal less damage whenever its hotbar is not active.
* Phoenix's [F] Swift Flight resembles [[Eagle]]'s [F] Flight.
* {{Ability|X}} can heal others even in [[Safe Zone]]. 
* Even if the player does not have 400  [[mastery]] on Phoenix, they can still participate in the raids.[[Raids|raid]]. 

